PR #233 reported zero barrier-arm walks and attributed them to the shipped
sanitizer vocabulary being crypto-only, concluding that "a sanitizer catalogue
is what arms" the removal-suppression hazard and therefore that gates should
land before catalogue growth.

The observation stands. The mechanism does not, and it was never established:
the zero was believed without a positive control — the rule this repo has
written down, violated the same day it was edited into the notebook.

Two purpose-built fixtures both produced ZERO walks:

  * `f = Fernet(key); plain = f.decrypt(tok); cipher = f.encrypt(plain)`
    emits `python:external:0-0:decrypt:external_symbol`. The receiver type is
    never inferred, so neither the plaintext SOURCE nor the `Fernet.encrypt`
    SANITIZER can match. No flow exists for a barrier to guard.
  * The same shape written module-qualified: source and sanitizer resolve, but
    the sink `pathlib.Path(...).write_text(x)` emits NO call edge — an
    attribute chain rooted at a CONSTRUCTOR RESULT. #231 fixed only chains
    rooted at a local; this sub-shape is still open and is filed on INV-mumov.

Every sanitizer in the catalogue is an INSTANCE METHOD (`Fernet.encrypt`,
`AESGCM.encrypt`, `AEAD.Seal`, `Cipher.doFinal`), so registering any barrier
needs precisely the receiver evidence that is missing. The barrier arm is
unreachable for the same root cause as the rest of this area — INV-linub — a
third symptom family alongside io-boundary catalogue reach and the §4 summary
lookup inside the walk.

Consequences, all filed on the items:

  * RECEIVER TYPING arms the suppression hazard, not catalogue growth.
    WI-joluk's gate landing first remains correct, for a sharper reason: the
    arming event is a specific blocking class item, not a diffuse trend.
  * INV-karud clause (b) is NOT independent corroboration. A sanitizer call
    site can only register if its callee resolves, so both zeros may share one
    upstream defect. Two instruments agreeing while sharing an upstream defect
    is agreement about the defect.
  * Still unresolved and stated rather than papered over: no positive control
    shows the barrier arm can fire in ANY configuration, and no end-to-end
    test drives it through `propagate_taint_ddg` — the one `sanitized` test
    uses `propagate_taint_structural`.

